   "source": [
    "# Experiment: Discrete vs Continuous (PGD) Adversarial Training\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research Question:** Does Continuous (PGD) adversarial training produce more profitable traders than Discrete adversarial training?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Extended Question:** Is more flexibility in discrete actions sufficient, or is continuous (PGD) truly necessary?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Version: 2.0 | Date: 2026-03-13 | Metric: PROFIT ONLY**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Goal\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare **THREE** adversarial training approaches:\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Approach | Description | Actions |\n",
    "|---|----------|-------------|---------|\n",
    "| 1 | **Discrete-4** | Current implementation (4 fixed actions: noise, bias, invert, none) | 4 discrete |\n",
    "| 2 | **Discrete-16** | Extended discrete with 16 actions (different strengths) | 16 discrete |\n",
    "| 3 | **Continuous (PGD)** | Gaussian policy with L2-norm clipping, perturbation per feature | Continuous vector |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hypothesis:** \n",
    "- If Discrete-16 ≈ Continuous → Flexibility is the key, not continuous space\n",
    "- If Continuous > Discrete-16 → Continuous space provides fundamental advantage\n",
    "- If all similar → Adversarial training method doesn't matter much\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Experiment Flow\n",
    "\n",
    "| Phase | What happens | Expected time |\n",
    "|-------|-------------|---------------|\n",
    "| Setup | Load data, create environments | 5 min |\n",
    "| Train Discrete-4 | Train trader with 4-action adversary | 1-2 hours |\n",
    "| Train Discrete-16 | Train trader with 16-action adversary | 1-2 hours |\n",
    "| Train Continuous | Train trader with PGD adversary | 1-2 hours |\n",
    "| Results | Compare profits | 5 min |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Configuration"
   ]
  },
